  "deletedBy": null,
  "details": "Ever since the avatar scaling feature came out, some worlds like Prison Escape and Hide And Shriek have taken it upon themselves to abuse these and added forced avatar scaling into their worlds. In the case of Prison Escape, the instance master can trigger this at will. None of these worlds give a warning that this can happen or ask for consent before doing it.\n\nThis poses a very serious physical safety concern, I've already seen one person that was a smaller avatar be force scaled into a much larger one and it caused them to be physically sick to the point where they were on the ground and had to get out of VR, because of the sudden change in view.\n\nThe ability to do this should be removed or at the very least, worlds should be required to have a warning and user consent. If the user doesn't want their scale changed, they should be given the option to decline and to leave the game or instance.",
